  TJJM gym-website overrides, file 4. Same format as files 1-3: ~Name|URL~
  An EMPTY value blanks the link. Only add an entry that CHANGES something.
  Rendered after file 3 by BOTH sections. Gate C3 still forbids a name in two files.

  15 Aug 2026 - BATCH 35. THE BROWSER RENDER PASS. 198 links that returned nothing to a
  plain HTTP fetch were opened in a real Chrome browser. Full write-up in
  region-rebuild-batch35-findings.md.

  *** THE HEADLINE: 'EMPTY' WAS NEVER A NEUTRAL VERDICT. ***
  We had been carrying these as 'unknown - needs a browser', assuming most were healthy
  JavaScript-rendered sites. They were not. 137 of 198 were broken - 69%, by far the
  worst rate of any screen in this programme. The dominant causes are mundane and
  invisible to a fetch: Wix 'domain not connected' placeholders, EXPIRED SQUARESPACE
  accounts, Flywheel and cPanel default pages, Cloudflare 1001/520/522 origin errors,
  and GoDaddy/Afternic '/lander' redirects. A fetch sees an empty body for all of them.

  VERDICTS: DEAD 80 | PARKED 37 | OK 61 | REPLACE 8 | WRONG_BUSINESS 7 | HIJACK 5

  LESSON FOR FUTURE SCREENS: treat EMPTY as SUSPECT, not as unknown. Any future row a
  fetch cannot read should go to a browser before the link is trusted, and if it cannot
  be browsed it is safer blanked than left live.

  TWO GATE C11 CATCHES WORTH RECORDING, both would have silently applied to nothing:
    'Chris Lisciandro's...'  the corpus spells it with a CURLY apostrophe U+2019
    'Dan Henderson's Athletic Fitness Center'  corpus name ends '- Formerly Team Quest'
  Two more were refused by C3 because batch 33 already handled them: UFC GYM Sunnyvale
  and UFC Gym Green Valley.

  ROW 198, 'GB Fulshear', WAS NOT RENDERED - the browser hit a hard safety block on the
  previous row and never recovered. It is untouched here. Batch 33 already repointed it.

